    {
      "t": "interlude",
      "text": "porthole",
      "sub": "the desk · the egg · the top floor · 2003",
      "duration": 2000
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "The desk lamp has a round brass shade. Up close it looks like a porthole."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Rivets around the rim. Thick glass."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol3_meld_time_pod_interior.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "cg",
      "src": "assets/cg/vol4_meld_facet_porthole.jpg",
      "caption": "the lamp, the porthole"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Jack Perkins sealed himself inside one quiet night and gestated in the time between times. All he dreamt of was home."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Through the glass, a room on a top floor. It is large for what it is, looks real nice and new and clean."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol3_hospital_room_window_night.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol3_hospital_hum.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "A television dangling from an odd angle plays video of ducks on a lake or a pond somewhere. It keeps going, so it is apparently a duck channel."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Andy falls asleep on the floor next to the air conditioning unit. This is something he did as a child. The hum, the constant mechanical breeze."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Dad turns away, watches the ducks."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol3_ballfield_dugout_august.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Great hit, he said."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol3_meld_time_pod_interior.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "bgm",
      "src": "assets/audio/bgm/vol4_cabin_hum.mp3"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Jack puts his hand flat on the glass."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "Could I save my father from death. Is there a way to let him know about the cancer before it is too late."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "The glass fogs with his breath. When it clears it's a lamp again, light on a page."
    },
    {
      "t": "bg",
      "src": "assets/backgrounds/vol4_desk_night.jpg"
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "I will love you forever, you know."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "You know."
    },
    {
      "t": "narrate",
      "text": "If it is 4am\nthen I am awake."
    },
    {
      "t": "flag",
      "key": "meld_facet_porthole",
      "val": true
    },
